/* scenes.js — the situations the town's generator draws from (generate.js; docs/05 §B1).

   A judgement question that only swaps a name or a number is the same question again, and a
   child who has met it once has met it. So each objective here has a POOL OF SITUATIONS:
   somebody in Bizzington, somewhere in it, doing one particular thing — the harbour at dawn,
   the bank steps, Mags's awning in the rain — and a question about that situation, with its
   own reason. Drawn from a seed, a question is a new situation, not new numbers in an old
   sentence.

   A four-option scene is [question, the right answer, three wrong ones, why]. The tokens are
   filled by generate.js from the seed:
     {w} {w2}   two different people of the town (Pip, Mags, Bea, Bo, Nana Bizz)
     {p} {P}    an amount, small and larger, priced in the child's own currency and sized to
                the maths she has met — always through money(), so My Feed prices it at render
   A typed scene is a function of the generator's kit and returns { q, value, why, hint }:
   its sum is worked here, so the answer is proved by the same code that asks it.

   THE MONEY RULES (CONCEPT §6) hold for every line: every amount is a story about the town,
   never a claim about the real world; a rate is "in a story" and "in every 100", never a
   percent a child has not met; the Exchange's companies are the game's own; borrowing is a
   tool with a price, never a moral failing; and nothing asks about a child's own household.
   Loaded only with generate.js — never on the first screen. */

